│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ## What needs to be migrated                                                                                                                    │
│ Python already has the middleware **core** (`MiddlewareStage`, phases, `MiddlewareRegistry`, `MiddlewareResult`, `InvokeModelStage`) in         │
│ `strands-py/src/strands/_middleware/`. Its README states the gap: *"Only `InvokeModelStage` is implemented. `ExecuteToolStage` and              │
│ `AgentStreamStage` will be added as needed."* This ports the two remaining stages **and** the middleware-initiated interrupt path.              │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ - **`ExecuteToolStage`** (`stages.ts:161`) — wraps a single tool execution. Context `ExecuteToolContext` (`stages.ts:104`): `{agent, tool:      │
│ Tool|undefined, toolUse, invocationState}` + extends `MiddlewareInterruptible`. Result `{result: ToolResultBlock}`. Supports short-circuit      │
│ (return a mock result without calling `next` → real tool doesn't run); hooks (`BeforeToolCallEvent`/`AfterToolCallEvent`) fire **outside**      │
│ middleware even on short-circuit.                                                                                                               │
│ - **`AgentStreamStage`** (`stages.ts:170`) — wraps the whole agent output stream (outermost). Context `{agent, args, options}` +                │
│ `MiddlewareInterruptible`. Marked `@internal` in TS (not in public `index.ts`) — keep it internal in Python too.                                │
│ - **Middleware interrupt path** — `MiddlewareInterruptResult<T> = {response: T}` wrapper; `MiddlewareInterruptible.interrupt()`;                │
│ `createMiddlewareInterrupt(interruptState, idPrefix)` factory (`agent.ts:368`), a **non-mutating** interrupt fn: id = `` `${idPrefix}:${name}`  │
│ ``; returns stored response on resume; honors preemptive `response`; else throws `InterruptError` with `source:'middleware'`.                   │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ## Python landing points                                                                                                                        │
│ - Stages → `strands-py/src/strands/_middleware/stages.py` (today only `InvokeModelStage`); export public ones from `_middleware/__init__.py`,   │
│ keep `AgentStreamStage` internal.                                                                                                               │
│ - `ExecuteToolStage` wiring → wrap the **core execution** segment of `ToolExecutor._stream` (`tools/executors/_executor.py:225-249`, the        │
│ `selected_tool.stream(...)` region) so `Before/AfterToolCallEvent` hooks stay outside middleware.                                               │
│ - `AgentStreamStage` wiring → wrap the per-invocation event-loop-cycle stream in `agent/agent.py` (`_run_loop` ~`1227`), hooks outside.         │
│ `self._middleware_registry` already exists (`agent.py:407`).                                                                                    │
│ - Interrupt path → reuse `strands-py/src/strands/interrupt.py` (`Interrupt`, `InterruptException`, `_InterruptState`) + `types/interrupt.py`    │
│ `_Interruptible`; add a `create_middleware_interrupt` factory returning the **wrapper** result (not the raw response).                          │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ## Gotchas / open questions (need maintainer input)                                                                                             │
│ - **Generator return values.** Python async generators can't `return` a value; Python already uses the *"last yielded event is the result"*     │
│ convention for `InvokeModelStage` (`event_loop.py:548`, `registry.py:83`). The two new stages must adopt it — pick the concrete terminal event  │
│ types.                                                                                                                                          │
│ - **`Interrupt.source` field is missing in Python** (`interrupt.py:22`). Porting `source:'middleware'` means adding a `source` field +          │
│ serialization — a cross-cutting change.                                                                                                         │
│ - **Python interrupts are tool-only today** (`event_loop.py:282`, resume keyed on tool_use/tool_results). An `AgentStreamStage` interrupt       │
│ doesn't fit that resume shape — expect to extend `_InterruptState.resume()`. **Deepest risk.**                                                  │
│ - **No public `addMiddleware` in Python** (TS has `Agent.addMiddleware`). The new stages are unusable without a registration entry point —      │
│ decide whether this port also adds one.                                                                                                         │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ## Completeness of source (strands-ts)                                                                                                          │
│ - Merged: ✅ (`ExecuteToolStage` `agent.ts:2517`, `AgentStreamStage` `agent.ts:1155`, `createMiddlewareInterrupt` `agent.ts:368`).              │
│ - Unit tests: ✅ (`middleware-interrupts.test.ts`, `agent-middleware.test.ts`, `copy-on-input.test.ts`, `custom-stages.test.ts`,                │
│ `registry.test.ts`).                                                                                                                            │
│ - Integ tests: ❌ none for middleware stages.                                                                                                   │
│ - Docs: ⚠️ no site/user-guide page; only `strands-ts/src/middleware/README.md` (design + behavioral spec). No user-facing docs to port.          │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ## Confirmation                                                                                                                                 │
│ -  The change is complete in the source SDK (merged + unit-tested); every related artifact is listed above. Test/doc caveats noted above.       │
